/-!
# Six-dimensional symmetric natural modules and rank-two involutions

The intrinsic binary symplectic type-a₂ conditions imply that each product
of the involution with a conjugate has order at most four. This bound and
the concrete permutation calculations exclude the natural normal A₇
extension and force transitivity on the moved plane in the eight-letter
case, including the index-two subgroup of the full split orthogonal group.
The source applications retain the actual group and module identifications
and discharge the conjugate-product premise of the original conditional APIs.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*,
G.11.2(4–5), printed p.364 (PDF p.375), and the proof of 6.2.19,
printed p.691 (PDF p.708). The general product-order theorem also supplies
the corresponding input to cases (6) and (7).
-/
